<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The iOS plist the shell merges over the generated one, named by
  `bundle.iOS.infoPlist` in tauri.conf.json.

  The CLI reads this file and merges it *into* the project's own
  `gen/apple/stvdy-shell_iOS/Info.plist`, so what lives here is only what the
  generated plist cannot express.

  **What is here, and what deliberately is not.**

  - `UIBackgroundModes` — `fetch` and `processing` are what make
    `BGAppRefreshTask` and `BGProcessingTask` schedulable at all (A315/A317);
    `remote-notification` is what lets an APNs silent push wake the app without a
    user-visible alert (A310). Without the array, `BGTaskScheduler.submit` fails at
    runtime with `BGTaskSchedulerErrorCodeUnavailable` and nothing in the build
    complains.
  - `BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers` — the two identifiers the app registers
    handlers for. A launch the scheduler woke for an identifier *not* in this list
    throws `NSInternalInconsistencyException` and the app is killed, so this list and
    the plugin's `scheduler.rs` constants are the same two strings and
    `tests/config.rs` compares them rather than trusting a comment.

  **The App Group is not here, and that is not an omission.** An App Group is an
  *entitlement* (`com.apple.security.application-groups`), not a plist key: it is
  declared on both targets in `gen/apple/project.yml.template` and XcodeGen writes it
  into the two `.entitlements` files. A plist key of that name would be ignored.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>fetch</string>
		<string>processing</string>
		<string>remote-notification</string>
	</array>
	<key>BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>app.stvdy.sync.refresh</string>
		<string>app.stvdy.sync.processing</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
